<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Document xmlns:p="property" xmlns:r="reflection" Id="JeWrzTOqz6yp29E1vz49ay" LanguageVersion="2025.7.4" Version="0.128">
  <NugetDependency Id="T5PXsPTxaPwby1BjID0HiN" Location="VL.CoreLib" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="Surf55RumayKAWe8QDa0w0" Location="VL.Skia" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="IHyuAlcj88cHv6LTqAKONL" Location="VL.Stride" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <Patch Id="NVE1SYhKnAVNr8ZjMH8IY3">
    <Canvas Id="D3BqoCSMXniGlr4w6M9r20" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="R3XaOAcG0Mq4HHYqblWLWx">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="HjBaQ7mBEySIeAbWCbhqpM">
        <Canvas Id="E90SEsDuO4d3hqM2INA5Ge" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="PCgXjIzm2jGRhVPs5ip1Z3" Bounds="-820,-60,680,700" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ACT IV LAB - Experiment: the globe, stage 2 step 2 - the view picks the tiles. NOT a shipped unit. Direction: docs/GLOBE-RESEARCH.md.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE QUESTION: the user's model of every map engine - 'only fetch the tiles the view can see' - on a sphere. Step 1 put 64 fixed tiles on the globe; this step lets the CAMERA decide: where it looks and how high it flies choose which tiles, at which zoom, are requested.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;HOW. The camera is vvvv's OrbitCamera (drag to orbit, wheel to approach). Its Position output is the only thing the selection reads: distance from the centre -&gt; height above the surface -&gt; ZOOM (clamped 3..11; height 2 is zoom 3, height 0.005 is zoom 11); the direction of the position -&gt; the longitude and latitude under the camera -&gt; the tile number at that zoom (forward Web Mercator, the formula of Tutorial 3.1). A 5 x 5 window of tiles around that number is requested; every tile whose URL changed is re-fetched, its old picture dropped, and drawn 3 mm above the base layer - the 64 zoom-3 tiles of step 1, always present, so the globe is never empty while detail arrives. Each detail tile is the same Plane + vertex-stage shader as step 1, with the window's zoom.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;FLIP FETCH ON, then approach a place with the wheel. ZOOM climbs, LON/LAT under the camera read out, DETAIL TILES READ counts the window's arrivals. The window always has 25 tiles; what changes is how much of the earth they cover.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;HONEST EDGES (this is a prototype of the IDEA, not of the engine):&#xD;&#xA;- no frustum culling: the window is 'around the point under the camera', not 'what the frustum sees', so at a grazing view the edges of the picture stay at zoom 3;&#xD;&#xA;- no cache: a tile that scrolls to another window slot is requested again; a real engine keys requests by tile number, not by slot - that is what a library's TileCache is for, and why this stays in the lab;&#xD;&#xA;- no hysteresis: at a zoom boundary a small movement re-requests all 25 tiles. OSM's policy tolerates a person at the wheel, not a script at the LFO;&#xD;&#xA;- the window does not wrap at the date line and is clamped at the poles.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Rules of the lab: no new library surface, fetch only on the toggle, results in docs/ACT-IV-LAB.md. Tiles (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; tile.openstreetmap.org usage policy applies (a User-Agent is sent).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
