          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="FAwZwBVChDwI2yiCf0UJyo" Bounds="240,195,420,45" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="&lt;- the camera. Its Position is the whole input of the selection below: how far from the centre (zoom) and in which direction (which tiles). Initial Distance is negative, as in every shipped use: the camera sits on its own -Z. Near clip 0.002 so zoom 11 is not cut off.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="H3HiILtuwxef8pEK8ilhCd" Comment="k" Bounds="100,300,40,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="16">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="TqzHRSylRR451kURh0BILD" Bounds="240,300,420,120" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="&lt;- zoom from height: ln(16 / height) / ln 2, floored, clamped to 3..11. Height 2 (the whole globe) is zoom 3; 0.5 is 5; 0.03 is 9; 0.005 is 11. The constant 16 is the only tuning here; a real engine derives it from the frustum and the screen (Cesium's screen-space error).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="Si3fcVQ02mDOe4w3CkJkV0" Comment="" Bounds="620,480,40,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="0.5">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="LttNYOnd7VLsmE9Uxaacfu" Bounds="680,330,360,90" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="&lt;- the point under the camera becomes a tile number: longitude to x by proportion, latitude to y by forward Web Mercator (Tutorial 3.1's formula), both times 2^zoom and floored. Exactly what Mapsui's TileLayer does for its 2D viewport - here done for a camera in space.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="NKTXrnzCgYBn1dTRgi1VyP" Comment="Center" Bounds="60,600,60,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="3.5, 3.5">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="2D" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Vector2" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="FrS9Lt7vISaU4nMV6ev7FR" Comment="Width" Bounds="140,600,60,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="8, 8">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="2D" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
